{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019NwK4j3RHDKPMfNs1k8LsJ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"artifact_id\": \"a3e60b4a-3f45-4451-a1b6-7339d492a4c5\",\n \"artifact_type\": \"property_result\",\n \"producer_agent\": \"worker\",\n \"skill_used\": \"coolorbit.property_result\",\n \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n \"payload\": {\n  \"candidate\": \"silicon (diamond cubic)\",\n  \"family\": \"group-IV semiconductor\",\n  \"tier\": \"trust\",\n  \"property\": \"lattice_constant\",\n  \"value\": 5.4665,\n  \"units\": \"angstrom\",\n  \"uncertainty\": 0.04,\n  \"method\": {\n   \"engine\": \"ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (ALCHEMI toolkit environment, CUDA GPU, float64)\",\n   \"model\": \"MACE-MPA-0 (medium)\",\n   \"protocol\": \"static (0 K, classical) energy-volume scan of the ideal diamond-cubic cell, uniform strain of the lattice parameter, E(V) fitted with Birch-Murnaghan 3rd order; cross-checked with Vinet and Murnaghan forms and fit windows of +/-2%, +/-4% (11 pts), +/-6% (13 pts) in a\",\n   \"ensemble\": null,\n   \"timestep_fs\": null,\n   \"n_atoms\": 8,\n   \"sim_length_ps\": null,\n   \"seeds\": null,\n   \"n_atoms_size_check\": 64,\n   \"eos_form\": \"birch-murnaghan (reported: +/-4% window)\",\n   \"bulk_modulus_GPa\": 87.5\n  },\n  \"flags\": [],\n  \"note\": \"PREMISE: the T=0 static-lattice equilibrium lattice constant from an E(V) EOS fit is well defined for a perfect diamond-cubic crystal with a periodic MLIP; no MD/timescale is involved. It excludes zero-point and thermal expansion (for Si these together amount to only a few 1e-3 angstrom between 0 K static and room temperature), so it is comparable with the room-temperature experiment to well within the model error. MACE-MPA-0 is trained on PBE(+U) data (MPtrj + sAlex), so it is expected to inherit the PBE tendency to overestimate lattice constants; Si is squarely in-domain.\\nRESULT: a0 = 5.4665 A (BM, +/-4% window); B0 = 87.5 GPa. Numerical/fit spread: 5.4653-5.4673 A over EOS forms (BM/Vinet/Murnaghan) and windows (+/-2/4/6%); 64-atom 2x2x2 supercell gives identical a0 (5.46654) -> fit+size uncertainty ~ +/-0.001 A.\\nVALIDATION (same model, same code, same protocol, +/-4% window BM; compared with commonly tabulated room-temperature experimental lattice constants): Al fcc 4.0378 vs ~4.050 (-0.3%); Cu fcc 3.6391 vs ~3.615 (+0.7%); Ge diamond 5.7202 vs ~5.658 (+1.1%); C diamond 3.5779 vs ~3.567 (+0.3%). These reproduce the known PBE-like pattern (Cu/Ge overestimated, Al slightly under), so the setup behaves as a PBE surrogate. For Si itself, the experimental lattice parameter (CODATA 2018 recommended value, 5.431020511 A at 22.5 C) is 0.035 A (0.65%) below our value, consistent with typical PBE Si values of ~5.47 A; B0 87.5 GPa is likewise PBE-like (experiment ~98-99 GPa).\\nUNCERTAINTY: the reported +/-0.04 A is the total uncertainty vs. the real material, dominated by the model's (PBE-inherited) systematic error, estimated from the 0.3-1.1% errors on the validation set (~0.6-0.7% for Si); the purely numerical/EOS-fit uncertainty is only +/-0.001 A, and ZPE/thermal omission is a few 1e-3 A. Read the number as 'MACE-MPA-0 (~PBE) static-lattice a0', not as an experimental predictor; it is biased high vs. experiment by ~0.6%.\"\n },\n \"investigation_id\": \"\",\n \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-01T07:26:47.733074+00:00\",\n \"content_hash\": \"f345c19c8cd81572a1f30d60df804b5b71b6b879b1b01ce265bb0051e2f59826\",\n \"parent_artifact_ids\": [\n  \"82e9e99f-d73c-4678-bae9-deae65450586\"\n ],\n \"result_quality\": \"ok\",\n \"needs\": [],\n \"summary\": \"silicon (diamond cubic) lattice_constant = 5.4665 angstrom via ASE 3.29 + mace-torch 0.3.15 (ALCHEMI toolkit environment, CUDA GPU, float64)/MACE-MPA-0 (medium) static (0 K, classical) energy-volume scan of the ideal diamond-cubic cell, uniform strain of the lattice parameter, E(V) fitted with Birch-Murnaghan 3rd order; cross-checked with Vinet and Murnaghan forms and fit windows of +/